        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Hidden data for JavaScript -->
      <script type="application/json" id="entry-data">
        {"id":"harvard_vi4_320","series":"Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)","seq":320,"text":"[[1388.9]] <b>264.  Deus nihil vult sine ratione [1678 bis 1681 (?)]</b>\n [[1388.10]] <tab/>[1678 bis 1681 (?)]\n[[1388.15]] <tit2><b>Deus nihil vult sine ratione</b></tit2> </p>\n<p> [[1388.16]] Probatur generaliter ex eo, quod nihil fit sine ratione. Nam nihil existit nisi omnia\n[[1388.17]] existant ad naturam ejus requisita. Omnium autem requisitorum existentiae simul sumtae\n[[1388.18]] sunt ratio rei. Ubi illud obiter notandum est si qua res non nisi unicum habeat requisitum\n[[1388.19]] seu naturae sit plane simplicis, eam rem si quidem existit, per se ipsam existere, id est\n[[1389.1]] esse necessariam, sive essentiam ejus involvere existentiam: sive rem ejusmodi habere\n[[1389.2]] rationem existendi in se ipsa. Nam sit res <i>A</i> cujus omnia requisita sint <i>b</i> et <i>c</i>, patet\n[[1389.3]] rationem existentiae <i>A</i> esse existentiam <i>b</i> + existentiam <i>c.</i> Sed si res <i>A</i> habeat unicum\n[[1389.4]] tantum requisitum <i>b</i>, patet <i>A</i> aequivalere ipsi <i>b</i>, quia in <i>A</i> nihil concipi potest praeter <i>b</i>,\n[[1389.5]] adeoque rationem existentiae ipsius <i>A</i> esse existentiam ipsius <i>b</i>, id est ipsius <i>A</i>; adeoque <i>A</i>\n[[1389.6]] sibi ipsi rationem esse existendi, sive necessario existere. </p>\n<p> [[1389.7]] Porro Dei voluntas non est necessaria, sed libera, id est pendet a consideratione finis\n[[1389.8]] sive boni. Et proinde voluntas habet requisita tum in Deo tum in idea objecti; in Deo\n[[1389.9]] omniscientiam, in idea objecti bonitatem seu aptitudinem ad fines a Deo propositos.\n[[1389.10]] Itaque dicere voluntatem aliquam sive in Deo, sive in aliquo alio, esse sine ratione, idem\n[[1389.11]] est ac dicere voluntatem in genere esse Ens per se, seu Ens carens requisitis. Sive Ens\n[[1389.12]] cujus conceptus sit irresolubilis. Cum tamen manifestum sit conceptum voluntatis esse\n[[1389.13]] resolubilem in alios conceptus. </p>\n<p> [[1389.14]] Non video quid haec opinio habeat duri. Nam utique in confesso est Deum semper\n[[1389.15]] eligere id quod est perfectissimum, quando unum ex eligibilibus est aliis perfectius, idque\n[[1389.16]] eum facere salva sua libertate. Ponamus ergo nunquam duas res aeque caeteris praestantes\n[[1389.17]] reperiri, sed semper unam aliis esse perfectiorem: quae Hypothesis certe nihil habet\n[[1389.18]] impossibile vel absurdum. Imo valde probabilis est, quia Essentiae rerum sunt ut numeri\n[[1389.19]] et non dantur duo Numeri aequales. Hac ergo hypothesi admissa, utique manifestum est\n[[1389.20]] quod diximus Deum nunquam quicquam facere sine ratione. </p>\n<p> [[1389.21]] Cartesius et Spinosa plane dissentiunt. Cartesius ait Deum non velle res quia sunt\n[[1389.22]] bonae, sed res intelligi bonas quia Deus vult. Quae opinio periculosissima est, sequitur\n[[1389.23]] enim nullam esse Dei justitiam sed stare voluntatem pro ratione. Spinosa ait eos longe\n[[1389.24]] minus errare, qui in Deo statuunt libertatem indifferentiae, quam qui putant Deum agere\n[[1389.25]] sub ratione boni. </p>\n","number":"264.","title":"Deus nihil vult sine ratione","date":"[1678 bis 1681 (?)]"}
      </script>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers using proper regex
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[([0-9]+\.[0-9]+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Get entry data from JSON script
    const entryDataScript = document.getElementById('entry-data');
    let entryData = null;
    if (entryDataScript) {
      try {
        entryData = JSON.parse(entryDataScript.textContent);
      } catch (e) {
        console.error('Failed to parse entry data:', e);
      }
    }

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entryData && entryData.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entryData.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>